1. POLICY CHECKPOINTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sixteen checkpoints across thirteen policies. Twelve are committed beside the
policy that loads them. Four are not, because their upstreams grant no licence
to redistribute them: ./download_weights.sh pulls those from the upstream
repository, so you take them under the upstream's terms rather than under this
repository's.

Four further rows are ONNX conversions, written by ./export_onnx.py from the
TorchScript checkpoints above them so that every policy can run on TensorRT.
A conversion is a derivative of its source and carries the source's terms
unchanged -- putting a weight in another container grants no right that did not
already exist. So each conversion ships exactly where its source ships: amo's
and rl_gym's are committed because their checkpoints are, and robomimic's is
generated on your machine because its checkpoint is fetched rather than
committed. Running robomimic therefore needs ./export_onnx.py after
./download_weights.sh; the other twelve policies need neither.

The sha256 column is the first four hex of the file's sha256 -- an identifier
for this table, not an integrity check. `sha256sum policies/*/model*` gives the
real thing. The twelve committed files verify against this record as committed,
and ./download_weights.sh carries the full sha256 of the other four and refuses
a download that does not match it.

